    <item>
      <title>Warsh Tells Traders to Watch the Data. They Still Follow the Fed</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-10-25/warsh-tells-traders-to-watch-the-data-they-still-follow-the-fed</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">97e4b85d45daeb1fa19712d3</guid>
      <pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Early on Oct. 14, just hours before the release of a much-anticipated report on US inflation, TD Securities’ Gennadiy Goldberg recommended that clients bet against a Federal Reserve interest-rate hike later in the month. The logic was that inflation would likely be benign enough to justify a hold. Equally important, a slew of Fed officials had spent days pushing back against expectations for an imminent move.</description>
      <dc:creator>Enda Curran, Ye Xie and Victor Swezey</dc:creator>
